35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The billing is area-based, not headcount. We pay for empty desks. This changes our cost calculus significantly.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Minato,,The window side is quieter. And my chair needs days to settle. Can we keep my spot stable?,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"@Minato, four to nine minutes daily is a huge hit. Plus, early birds grab the good spots before we even arrive.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the badge data confirms it. First-come, first-served is rigged. We need a fixed assignment, not a daily scramble.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shunichi, fixed seats help. But last spring, proximity made us talk more. I worry we lose that if we just assign spots.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, fixed seats solve the scramble, but the 6,200 yen per move means we must finalize the layout now to avoid recurring costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, six thousand yen is a lot. But if the window side is quiet, is it worth it for my back?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, six thousand yen is fine if it saves my morning. I need a fixed spot so I don’t waste time hunting for a desk.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, cost is secondary to fairness. The shuffles prove the current chaos is accidental. We need to explicitly assign the worse spots, not let them drift.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Victoria, the cost is real. But the joiners learned by overhearing. If we isolate them, we lose that.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, isolation is a risk, but the 41,000 yen monthly waste is undeniable. We must optimize for cost efficiency first.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I understand the cost. But my body needs the quiet window side. Can we please write that comfort down?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Victoria, cost is secondary to my sanity. I need a fixed, efficient spot to protect my gaps.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, efficiency ignores the human cost. The shuffles show we’ve never explicitly assigned the bad spots. We must decide who takes the hit, not let it drift.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Victoria, I hear the cost. But if we isolate the new joiners, they lose the chance to learn by listening.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I acknowledge the human costs, but the budget is fixed. We cannot afford inefficiency. Let us proceed to the options.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Minato,,I just want the quiet window side. Please write down that comfort matters.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,I’m done arguing. I just need a fixed spot that protects my gaps. Let’s see the options.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I’m done debating. The data is clear: we need explicit assignments. Let’s see the options and stop letting habit decide who suffers.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I’m still quiet. I just want us to keep talking. Let’s see the options.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
